  ("N1" "TENE, hold: with load at 1, q' is d; with load at 0, q' is q, and q keeps its bit for as long as it likes.")
  ("N2" "Given every gate proven and ELIGE. A gate reads the flip-flop as it reads a switch: the loop runs through the clock, never around it.")
  ("N3" "Rem tene, verba sequentur, said Cato: hold the matter and the words will follow. Hold the bit, and the memory will."))
